### Slot lookup (same request the REST Connector sends)
GET http://localhost:8090/scheduling/api/v1/slots?department=GENERAL_MEDICINE&date=2026-11-05&session=MORNING

### No slots (dermatology is fully booked in the mock)
GET http://localhost:8090/scheduling/api/v1/slots?department=DERMATOLOGY&date=2026-11-05&session=ANY

### Booking (what the appointment.request-booking worker sends)
POST http://localhost:8090/scheduling/api/v1/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

< ./booking.request.json

### Start a request through the lab app
POST http://localhost:8093/api/process-instances
Content-Type: application/json

< ./start-instance.request.json

### Start through the Camunda 8 REST API (v2)
POST http://localhost:8080/v2/process-instances
Content-Type: application/json

< ./camunda-rest-create-instance.request.json

### Scheduling outage on / off
PUT http://localhost:8090/admin/faults/scheduling?mode=DOWN
###
PUT http://localhost:8090/admin/faults/scheduling?mode=UP

### Live results table
GET http://localhost:8093/api/scenarios/results.md
